INSERT INTO content_raw_archive ("id", "block_id", "raw_text", "repaired_text", "created_at") VALUES (157, 157, 'An electric iron consumes energy at a rate of 840 W when heating is
at the maximum rate and 360 W when the heating is at the minimum.
The voltage is 220 V . What ar e the curr ent and the r esistance in each
case?
From Eq. (11.19), we know that the power input is
P = V I

Thus the current I = P/V

(a)When heating is at the maximum rate,

I = 840 W/220 V = 3.82 A;

and the resistance of the electric iron is

R = V/I = 220 V/3.82 A = 57.60 Ω.

(b)When heating is at the minimum rate,

I = 360 W/220 V = 1.64 A;

and the resistance of the electric iron is

R = V/I = 220 V/1.64 A = 134.15 Ω.', 'An electric iron consumes energy at a rate of 840 W when heating is at the maximum rate and 360 W when the heating is at the minimum. The voltage is 220 V. What are the current and the resistance in each case? From Eq. (11.19), we know that the power input is P = V I. Thus the current I = P/V.

